# The slow checks, run once before the code leaves this machine rather than on
# every commit.
#
# These are the same two things CI runs first, so a red pipeline is something
# you find out about in thirty seconds locally instead of three minutes later
# in a browser tab. Neither needs credentials or a network.
#
# `main` deploys to production on push, which is the other reason this exists
# here rather than only in CI: by the time CI goes red on main, Vercel is
# already building.
npm run typecheck
npm run check:launch
